const faqs = [
  { q: 'Why run Google Ads at all?', a: "Because the people on Google typed it in. \"Water heater replacement near me.\" \"Invisalign cost.\" \"LTL freight broker Dallas.\" They're not browsing. They're hiring. If you're not there when they search, your competitor is. Google is the fastest way we know to get the phone ringing this month." },
  { q: 'How is Google Ads different from SEO?', a: "Google Ads is paid. You show up above the free results and pay for each click, starting the day you turn it on. SEO is earning the free spots, and it takes months. We do both. Ads for this month, SEO for next year." },
  { q: 'What does Google Ads cost?', a: "You pay per click, and the price depends on how many businesses in your market want the same search. On a call we figure out what a lead is worth to you first, then set a cost cap so Google only spends when it can get a lead for about that much. Our guarantee needs $3,000 a month in ad spend to work. That's the floor." },
